#. Tag: title
#: developers-plugins.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Developing &krita; Plugins"
msgstr "ការអភិវឌ្ឍន​កម្មវិធី​ជំនួ​យ​របស់ &krita; "

#. Tag: title
#: developers-plugins.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "សេចក្ដី​ណែនាំ"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krita; is infinitely extensible with plugins. Tools, filters, large chunks "
"of the user interface and even colorspaces are plugins. In fact, &krita; "
"recognizes these six types of plugins:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:14
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"colorspaces &mdash; these define the channels that constitute a single pixel"
msgstr "&mdash; ឆានែល a ទោល"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:16
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "tools &mdash; anything that is done with a mouse or tablet input device"
msgstr "&mdash; អ្វី​ទាំងអស់ ជា ធ្វើរួច ដោយ a កណ្ដុរ ឬ ឧបករណ៍"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:18
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "paint operations &mdash; pluggable painting effects for tools"
msgstr "&mdash; ការ​គូរ សម្រាប់"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:20
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"image filters &mdash; change all pixels, or just the selected pixels in a "
"layer"
msgstr "រូបភាព&mdash; ទាំងអស់ ភីកសែល ឬ ភីកសែល អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ a"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:22
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"viewplugins &mdash; extend Krita’s user interface with new dialog boxes, "
"palettes and operations"
msgstr "&mdash; Krita វិ. អ្នក​ប្រើ ដោយ និង"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:24
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "import/export filters &mdash; read and write all kinds of image formats"
msgstr "&mdash; និង ទាំងអស់ រូបភាព"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:28
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krita; itself consists of three layered libraries and a directory with some "
"common support classes: kritacolor, kritaimage and kritaui. Within &krita;, "
"objects can by identified by a <classname>KisID</classname>, that is the "
"combination of a unique untranslated string (used when saving, for instance) "
"and a translated string for GUI purposes."
msgstr ""
"&krita; និង a ដោយ និង&krita; a<classname></classname> ជា a សម្រាប់ និង a សម្រាប់ "
"GUI."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:34
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A word on compatibility: &krita; is still in development. From &krita; 1.5 "
"to 1.6 not many API changes are expected, but there may be some. From "
"&krita; 1.6 to 2.0 we will move from &Qt;3 to &Qt;4, from &kde;3 to &kde;4, "
"from <command>automake</command> to <command>cmake</command>: many changes "
"are to be expected. If you develop a plugin for &krita; and choose to do so "
"in &krita;’s subversion repository, chances are excellent that we’ll help "
"you porting. These changes may also render parts of this document out of "
"date. Always check with the latest API documentation or the header files "
"installed on your system."
msgstr ""
"A&krita; ជា អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ ពី&krita; ដល់ ពី&krita; ដល់ ពី&Qt; ដល់&Qt; ពី&kde; ដល់&kde; "
"ពី<command></command> ដល់<command></command> ដល់ a កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ សម្រាប់&krita; និង ដល់ "
"អ៊ិន្ឈ៍&krita; វិ. ជំនួយ កាល​បរិច្ឆេទ ជានិច្ច ដោយ ឬ ប្រព័ន្ធ​."

#. Tag: title
#: developers-plugins.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "KritaColor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:49
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first library is kritacolor. This library loads the colorspace plugins."
msgstr "ទី​មួយ ជា."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:51
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A colorspace plugin should implement the <classname>KisColorSpace</"
"classname> abstract class or, if the basic capabilities of the new "
"colorspace will be implemented by <command>lcms</command> (<ulink url="
"\"http://www.littlecms.com/\"></ulink>), extend "
"<classname>KisAbstractColorSpace</classname>. The kritacolor library could "
"be used from other applications and does not depend on &koffice;."
msgstr ""
"A កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ<classname></classname> ឬ<command></command><ulink url=\"http://"
"www.littlecms.com/\"></ulink><classname></classname> ពី និង&koffice;."

#. Tag: title
#: developers-plugins.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "KritaImage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:63
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The libkritaimage library loads the filter and paintop plugins and is "
"responsible for working with image data: changing pixels, compositing and "
"painting. Brushes, palettes, gradients and patterns are also loaded by "
"libkritaimage. It is our stated goal to make libkritaimage independent of "
"&koffice;, but we currently share the gradient loading code with &koffice;."
msgstr ""
"និង និង ជា សម្រាប់ ដោយ រូបភាព ភីកសែល និង ការ​គូរ និង បានផ្ទុក​ ជា ដល់&koffice; "
"ដោយ&koffice;."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:69
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is not easy at the moment to add new types of resources such as brushes, "
"palettes, gradients or patterns to &krita;. (Adding new brushes, palettes, "
"gradients and patterns is easy, of course.) &krita; follows the guidelines "
"of the Create project (<ulink url=\"http://create.freedesktop.org/\"></"
"ulink>) for these. Adding support for Photoshop's brush file format needs "
"libkritaimage hacking; adding more gimp brush data files not."
msgstr ""
"ជា នៅ ដល់ ឬ ដល់&krita; និង ជា&krita; បង្កើត<ulink url=\"http://create."
"freedesktop.org/\"></ulink> សម្រាប់ សម្រាប់ វិ.."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "<classname>KritaImage</classname> loads the following types of plugins:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:81
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krita; filters must extend and implement the abstract class "
"<classname>KisFilter</classname>, <classname>KisFilterConfiguration</"
"classname> and possibly <classname>KisFilterConfigurationWidget</classname>. "
"An example of a filter is Unsharp Mask."
msgstr ""
"&krita; និង<classname></classname><classname></classname> និង<classname></"
"classname> a ជា របាំង."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:86
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Paint operations or paintops are the set of operations painting tools suchs "
"as freehand or circle have access to. Examples of paintops are pen, airbrush "
"or eraser. Paintops should extend the <classname>KisPaintop</classname> base "
"class. Examples of new paintops could be a chalk brush, an oilpaint brush or "
"a complex programmable brush."
msgstr "ឬ ការ​គូរ ឬ រង្វង់​ ដល់ ឧទាហរណ៍ ឬ<classname></classname> មូលដ្ឋាន ឧទាហរណ៍ a ឬ a."

#. Tag: title
#: developers-plugins.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "KritaUI"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:99
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The libkritaui library loads the tool and viewplugins. This library is a "
"&koffice; Part, but also contains a number of widgets that are useful for "
"graphics applications. Maybe we will have to split this library in kritapart "
"and kritaui in the 2.0 release. For now, script writers are not given access "
"to this library and plugin writers are only allowed to use this library when "
"writing tools or viewplugins. <classname>KritaUI</classname> loads the "
"following types of plugins:"
msgstr ""
"និង ជា a&koffice; មាន a លេខ​ សម្រាប់ ក្រាហ្វិក ដល់ អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ និង អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ ចេញ​ផ្សាយ សម្រាប់ ឥឡូវ ស្គ្រីប​ "
"ដល់ និង កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ ដល់ ឬ<classname></classname>:"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:110
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tools are derived from <classname>KisTool</classname> or one of the "
"specialized tool base classes such as <classname>KisToolPaint</classname>, "
"<classname>KisToolNonPaint</classname> or <classname>KisToolFreehand</"
"classname>. A new tool could be a foreground object selection tool. Painting "
"tools (and that includes tools that paint on the selection) can use any "
"paintop to determine the way pixels are changed."
msgstr ""
"ឧបករណ៍ ពី<classname></classname> ឬ មួយ មូលដ្ឋាន<classname></"
"classname><classname></classname> ឬ<classname></classname> A a និង ដល់ ភីកសែល."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:117
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Viewplugins are ordinary KParts that use <command>kxmlgui</command> to "
"insinuate themselves into &krita;'s user interface. Menu options, dialogs, "
"toolbars &mdash; any kind of user interface extension can be a viewplugin. "
"In fact, important functionality like &krita;'s scripting support is written "
"as a viewplugin."
msgstr ""
"<command></command> ដល់&krita; វិ. អ្នក​ប្រើ ម៉ឺនុយ&mdash; អ្នក​ប្រើ a ក្នុង&krita; វិ. ជា "
"a."

#. Tag: title
#: developers-plugins.docbook:127 developers-plugins.docbook:882
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Import/Export filters"
msgstr "នាំចូល នាំចេញ"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:129
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Import/Export filters are &koffice; filters, subclasses of "
"<classname>KoFilter</classname>. Filters read and write image data in any of "
"the myriad image formats in existence. And example of a new &krita; import/"
"export filter could be a PDF filter. Filters are loaded by the &koffice; "
"libraries."
msgstr ""
"នាំចូល នាំចេញ&koffice;<classname></classname> តម្រង និង រូបភាព អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ រូបភាព អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ "
"a&krita; a តម្រង បានផ្ទុក​&koffice;."

#. Tag: title
#: developers-plugins.docbook:142
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Creating plugins"
msgstr "កំពុង​បង្កើត"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:144
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Plugins are written in C++ and can use all of &kde; and &Qt; and the &krita; "
"developer API. Only viewplugins should use the &koffice; API. Don’t worry: "
"&krita;’s API’s are quite clear and rather extensively documented (for free "
"software) and coding your first filter is really easy."
msgstr ""
"កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ C និង ទាំងអស់&kde; និង&Qt; និង&krita; អ្នក​អភិវឌ្ឍន៍ តែ​មួយ&koffice;&krita; "
"វិ. វិ. និង សម្រាប់ និង ទី​មួយ ជា."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:149
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not want to use C++, you can write scripts in Python or Ruby; that "
"is a different thing altogether, though, and you cannot currently write "
"tools, colorspaces, paintops or import/export filters as scripts."
msgstr "ដល់ C អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ ឬ ជា a និង ឬ."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:153
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krita; plugins use &kde;'s parts mechanism for loading, so the parts "
"documentation at <ulink url=\"http://developer.kde.org\"></ulink> is "
"relevant here, too."
msgstr ""
"&krita;&kde; វិ. សម្រាប់ នៅ<ulink url=\"http://developer.kde.org\"></ulink> ជា."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:156
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your distribution should have either installed the relevant header files "
"with &krita; itself, or might have split the header files into either a "
"&koffice; dev or a &krita; dev package. You can find the API documentation "
"for &krita;'s public API at <ulink url=\"http://koffice.org/developer/"
"apidocs/krita/html/\"></ulink>."
msgstr ""
"ការ​ចែកចាយ ដោយ&krita; ឬ a&koffice; ឬ a&krita; អ្នក សម្រាប់&krita; វិ. នៅ<ulink "
"url=\"http://koffice.org/developer/apidocs/krita/html/\"></ulink>."

#. Tag: title
#: developers-plugins.docbook:164
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Automake (and CMake)"
msgstr "និង"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:166
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; 3.x and thus &koffice; 1.5 and 1.6 use <command>automake</command>; "
"&kde; 4.0 and &koffice; 2.0 use <command>cmake</command>. This tutorial "
"describes the <command>automake</command> way of creating plugins."
msgstr ""
"&kde; x និង&koffice; និង<command></command>&kde; និង&koffice;<command></"
"command> ឯកសារ​បង្រៀន<command></command>."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:172
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Plugins are &kde; modules and should be tagged as such in their "
"<filename>Makefile.am</filename>. Filters, tools, paintops, colorspaces and "
"import/export filters need <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"files; viewplugins need a <application>KXMLGui</application> "
"<filename>pluginname.rc</filename> file in addition. The easiest way to get "
"started is to checkout the krita-plugins project from the &koffice; "
"Subversion repository and use it as the basis for your own project. We "
"intend to prepare a skeleton &krita; plugin pack for KDevelop, but haven’t "
"had the time to do so yet."
msgstr ""
"កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ&kde; និង អ៊ិន្ឈ៍<filename> ព្រឹក</filename> តម្រង និង<literal role="
"\"extension\"> ផ្ទៃតុ</literal> a<application></application><filename></"
"filename> អ៊ិន្ឈ៍ ដល់ ជា ដល់ ពី&koffice; និង សម្រាប់ ដល់ a&krita; កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ សម្រាប់ ពេល​"
"វេលា ដល់."

#. Tag: filename
#: developers-plugins.docbook:185
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Makefile.am"
msgstr "ព្រឹក"

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:187
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's look at the skeleton for a plugin module. First, the "
"<filename>Makefile.am</filename>. This is what &kde; uses to generate the "
"makefile that builds your plugin: <programlisting>\n"
"kde_services_DATA = kritaLIBRARYNAME.desktop\n"
"\n"
"INCLUDES = $(all_includes)\n"
"\n"
"kritaLIBRARYNAME_la_SOURCES = sourcefile1.cc sourcefile2.cc\n"
"\n"
"kde_module_LTLIBRARIES = kritaLIBRARYNAME.la\n"
"noinst_HEADERS = header1.h header2.h\n"
"\n"
"kritaLIBRARYNAME_la_LDFLAGS = $(all_libraries) -module $(KDE_PLUGIN)\n"
"kritaLIBRARY_la_LIBADD = -lkritacommon\n"
"\n"
"kritaextensioncolorsfilters_la_METASOURCES = AUTO\n"
"</programlisting> This is the makefile for a filter plugin. Replace "
"<replaceable>LIBRARYNAME</replaceable> with the name of your work, and you "
"are set."
msgstr ""
"វិ. នៅ សម្រាប់ a កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ ម៉ូឌុល<filename> ព្រឹក</filename> ជា&kde; ដល់ កម្មវិធី​"
"ជំនួយ<programlisting> ផ្ទៃតុ n ទាំងអស់ n n ម៉ូឌុល ម៉. ម៉. n ទាំងអស់ ម៉ូឌុល KDE n ស្វ័យប្រវត្តិ\n"
"</programlisting> ជា សម្រាប់ a កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ ជំនួស​<replaceable></replaceable> ដោយ "
"ឈ្មោះ និង."

#. Tag: para
#: developers-plugins.docbook:197
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your plugin is a viewplugin, you will likely also install a <literal role="
"\"extension\">.rc</literal> file with entries for menubars and toolbars. "
"Likewise, you may need to install cursors and icons. That is all done "
"through the ordinary &kde; <filename>Makefile.am</filename> magic "
"incantantions:"
msgstr ""
"កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ ជា a a<literal role=\"extension\"></literal> ដោយ សម្រាប់ និង ដល់ និង រូប​"
"តំណាង ជា ទាំងអស់ ធ្វើរួច&kde;<filename> ព្រឹក</filename>:"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: developers-plugins.docbook:203
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"kritarcdir = $(kde_datadir)/krita/kritaplugins\n"
"kritarc_DATA = LIBRARYNAME.rc\n"
"EXTRA_DIST = $(kritarc_DATA)\n"
"\n"
"kritapics_DATA = \\\n"
"   bla.png \\\n"
"   bla_cursor.png\n"
"kritapicsdir = $(kde_datadir)/krita/pics"
msgstr ""
"n\n"
"\n"
" ទស្សន៍​ទ្រនិច"

